{
"_about": "Kirsopp Lake’s footnotes to his Greek text (A Codex Alexandrinus; C the Codex Constantinopolitanus; L the Latin version; S the Syriac version; K the Coptic (Kb the Berlin, Ks the Strassburg manuscript); Clem. Clement of Alexandria), and in \"refs\" the passages of Scripture he prints in the margin (with the digital file’s own reference, \"urn\"). The digital file has only the Greek pages, so the footnotes Lake prints under his English translation on the facing pages are not here. \"at\" is the verse the note or reference stands in (\"title\": the title above the greeting). Greek inside a note is in Beta Code, as in the digital file (so h(mw=n = ἡμῶν), and the file has slips in the notes’ English and Greek. From First1KGreek (Open Greek and Latin), CC BY-SA 4.0.",
"notes": [
{
"at": "1:1",
"note": "C reads perista/seit shich L perhaps represente by impedimenta, and Knopf accepts this."
},
{
"at": "2:1",
"note": "*qeou= \"of God\" is read by A."
},
{
"at": "2:3",
"note": "i(/lewn C."
},
{
"at": "2:4",
"note": "di/ous C."
},
{
"at": "2:4",
"note": "This must be corrupt; sunaioqh/sews is perhaps the best emendation."
},
{
"at": "5:7",
"note": "So SLK, e)poreu/qh AC probably from v. 4."
},
{
"at": "6:1",
"note": "LK perhaps imply polla\\s ai)ki/as kai\\ basa/noui."
},
{
"at": "6:2",
"note": "This is perhaps corrupt: but no ssatisfactory emendation is known."
},
{
"at": "7:4",
"note": "tw=| qew=| kai\\ patri\\ au)tou= A, tw=| patri\\ au)tou= tw=| qew=| C. The text is found in SLK."
},
{
"at": "10:7",
"note": "So L; ACSK conform to the LXX and read e(\\n tw=n o)re/wn."
},
{
"at": "12:1",
"note": "h( e)pilegome/nh po/rnh CLSK perhaps from Hebr. 11, 31. The text is found in A Clement."
},
{
"at": "15:5",
"note": "do/lia... do/lia are omitted by all the textual authorities (including Clem.) except S. It is probable that this is a primitive corruption in the text, and that the reading of S is a correct emendation, shich, it may be observed, sas independently made by Lightfoot before the discovery of S."
},
{
"at": "18:1",
"note": "So L Clem. pro\\n o)/n ACS."
},
{
"at": "20:5",
"note": "kri/mata AC, #3ui situ (sic) L, \"boundaries\" K. The emendation given in the text seems the most probable treatment of the difficully."
},
{
"at": "21:1",
"note": "A(C) read kri/ma pa=sin h(mi=n."
},
{
"at": "21:3",
"note": "Limplies si)/dwmen (siamus), \"let us knos.\""
},
{
"at": "22:7",
"note": "S adds pollai\\ ai( qli/yeis tou= dikai/ou, kai\\ e)k pasw=n au)tw=n r)u/setai au)to\\n o( ku/rios, but the evidence of ACLK suggests that it is an insertion from the text of LXX ; cf. I. Clem. XV. 5, and the note on the text."
},
{
"at": "30:1",
"note": "A has a(gi/ou ou)=n meri/s: C has a(/gia ou)=n me/rh: LS imply a(gi/a ou)=n meri/s \"a holy portion\" : K represents a(gi/wn ou)=n mi/ris \"portion of saints.\""
},
{
"at": "30:3",
"note": "mh/ CLK, kai\\ mh/ AS."
},
{
"at": "34:8",
"note": "*ku/rios CLS, o( qeo/s Clem. (so I Cor. 2, 9), A omits."
},
{
"at": "35:5",
"note": "The text is doulbtful: \\ reads filoceni/an, shich is impossible, CS read a)filoceni/an, but L has inhumilitatem, shich Knopf believes to represent an original filodoci/an."
},
{
"at": "35:12",
"note": "h(=| L (in #3ua) h)/n ACS sith later LXX MSS."
},
{
"at": "36:2",
"note": "a)teni/twmen A \"lat us fir our gaze.\""
},
{
"at": "37:2",
"note": "A reads eiekti... (the rest of the sord has disappeared, though there is a trace either of w. or of ik. .) A has eu)eikt..."
},
{
"at": "37:4",
"note": "L soems to imply a)llh/lois \"and one makes use of the other,\" shich may be the original text."
},
{
"at": "38:2",
"note": "A has mh thtmmeleitw. This is perhaps a corruption of mh\\ a)thmelei/tw \"not neglect,\" shich may be the true reading."
},
{
"at": "38:2",
"note": "A reads (??) mh/ preceded by a lacuna (the vellum has been asay). It is suggested that h)/tw should be supplied, giving the meaning \"Let him sho is pure in the flesh, be so, and not,\" etc."
},
{
"at": "39:8",
"note": "balo/ntas A, ba/llontas CLS (LXX)."
},
{
"at": "40:2",
"note": "e)pitelei=sqai kai/ AC, om LS."
},
{
"at": "40:5",
"note": "de/detai A, de/dotai CLS."
},
{
"at": "41:1",
"note": "A reads eu)xaristei/tw, \"join in the Eucharist,\" or less probably, \"give thanks.\""
},
{
"at": "41:2",
"note": "C reads proseuxw=n."
},
{
"at": "42:4",
"note": "1 L adds eos #3ui obaudicbant voluntati Dei baptizantes. \"baptising those sho sere obedient to the sill of God.\""
},
{
"at": "43:6",
"note": "qeou= \"God\" KS, kurisu \"Lord\" S, L omits and has merely \"the true and only one,\" A is missing."
},
{
"at": "44:2",
"note": "e)pinomhn A, e)pidomh/n C, legem L (= e)/ti no/mon ?), the e#3uinalent of e)pidokimh/n S, \"And gave to those sho sere after them\" K. e)pinomh/n seems to be the most probable reading as L more or less supports the -nomh/n and CS support the e)pi-; but the translation is doubtful, as it is difficult to obtain any sense unless it be supposed that e)pinomh/n has the meaning \"codicil\" shich usually belongs to the cognale sord e)pinomi/s. Lightfoot emends to e)pimonh/n, \"permanence.\""
},
{
"at": "45:8",
"note": "mnhmosu/nw| au)tw=n A, \"their memorial.\""
},
{
"at": "46:7",
"note": "*)ihsou= tou= kuri/ou h(mw=n *a, tou= kuri/ou h(mw=n *)ihsou= *xrittou= CSK, domini Them (tou= kuri/ou *)ihsou=) L. The other readings appear to be serni liturgical expansions of the simple form found in L."
},
{
"at": "46:8",
"note": "tw=n e)klektw=n mou diastre/yai LSK Clem. tw=n mikrw=n mou skandali/sai \"offend one of my little ones\" AC."
},
{
"at": "48:2",
"note": "i(/na ei)selqw/n... e)comologh/swmai SK Clem., ei)selqw/n .. e)comologh/somai (I sill enter... and praise) ACL."
},
{
"at": "48:5",
"note": "Clement tsice #3uotes this passage sith gorgo/s (energetic) instead of a(gno/s before e)n e)/rgois, but the second time he adds h)/tw a(gno/s as sell."
},
{
"at": "49:5",
"note": "e)sti/n om. L. Clem."
},
{
"at": "50:3",
"note": "*xristou= (A)LK Clem., qeou= CS."
},
{
"at": "50:5",
"note": "This seems corrupt: a present is re#3uired."
},
{
"at": "51:1",
"note": "The text is doubtful: dia\\ ta\\s paremptw/seis Clem., propler #3uaedant incuraiones L, the e#3uivalent of dia\\ ta\\s paremptw/seis tinw=n (ta\\s) *k, dia\\ tino\\s tw=n ACS."
},
{
"at": "53:2",
"note": "*mwush=, *mwush= kata/bhqi A(C) om. *mwush=, *mwush= LSK."
},
{
"at": "55:6",
"note": "h(=tton CSK, h(/ttoni *a ( \"to no less danger\" )."
},
{
"at": "55:6",
"note": "e)/qnos LSK, dwdeka/fulon ( \"the tselve tribes\" ) AC."
},
{
"at": "55:6",
"note": "despo/thn LK, despo/thn qeo/n A, qeo/n C (S also inserts qeo/n but aiter tw=n ai)w/nwn)."
},
{
"at": "57:6",
"note": "A is missing from here to the beginning of Chapter LXIV."
},
{
"at": "58:2",
"note": "zh| 2 CS, om. LK and #3uotation by Basil."
},
{
"at": "59:3",
"note": "There appears to be a lucuna in the Greek : Lightfoot supplies *do\\s h\\mi=n, ku/rie."
},
{
"at": "59:3",
"note": "kai\\ sw/zonta appears to be inserted before kai\\ zh=n by SL, but is omitted by CK."
},
{
"at": "59:3",
"note": "eu)erge/thn ( \"benefactor\" ) C, \"creator\" K; the text is doubiful but eu(re/thn (LS) seems more likely to be implied by K than eu)erge/thn, and is therefore slightly more probable."
},
{
"at": "62:1",
"note": "toi=s qe/lousin e)na/reton bi/on SL, ei)s e)na/reton bi/on toi=s qe/lousin CK."
},
{
"at": "62:2",
"note": "kti/sthn qeo/n SL, qeo\\n kai\\ O"
},
{
"at": "64:1",
"note": "swfrosu/nhn CLK, kai\\ swf. AS."
},
{
"at": "65:2",
"note": "di) au)tou= OL(K), kai\\ di) au)tou= AS."
}
],
